    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Postdoctoral-Researcher---Electrical--Computer-and-Telecommunications-Engineering-Technology--ECTET-_JR103437": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher - Electrical, Computer and Telecommunications Engineering Technology (ECTET)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-16\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAppointment: Full-time, 12-18 months (flexible time duration) Position Summary: The Postdoctoral Researcher will conduct research and development in advanced power electronics and energy conversion systems, with an emphasis on high-power back-to-back converters, solid state transformer technologies. The researcher will work under the supervision of Dr. Liwei Zhou at Rochester Institute of Technology. The research program focuses on developing and integrating back-to-back power converter technology, and advancing an integrated Solid-State Transformer architecture. The project will involve close collaboration with graduate students, industry partners, and external engineering/manufacturing collaborators. Primary Responsibilities: Develop models, control algorithms, and experimental platforms for high-power back-to-back power converters. Support integration of back-to-back converter and DAB stages toward a Solid-State Transformer system. Design, implement, and test power converter control algorithms, including active front-end and rectifier control. Integrate power electronic hardware, sensors, filters, control interfaces, and protection systems. Perform experimental characterization, data analysis, troubleshooting, and performance evaluation of converter prototypes. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics, Power Engineering, or a closely related field, completed by the appointment start date. Strong background in power electronics and power converter systems. Experience with modeling, simulation, control, and experimental validation of power electronic converters. Experience with MATLAB/Simulink or comparable modeling and control-development tools. Experience with laboratory testing of power electronic hardware. Strong technical communication and documentation skills. Preferred Qualifications: Research experience with one or more of the following: DC/AC inverters, Dual Active Bridge converters, Solid-State Transformers, grid-connected power converters, or high-power DC/DC converters. Experience with real-time control platforms, rapid-control-prototyping systems, DSPs, FPGAs, or similar embedded-control hardware. Experience with high-voltage/high-power laboratory testing, sensing, protection, and hardware integration. Demonstrated research productivity through peer-reviewed publications, patents, or significant prototype development.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Independently conducts research including, but not limited to, constructing hypotheses, design and planning of research studies, data management, model development, conducting experiments or assessments, analysis and interpretation of results, and evaluation of research techniques Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders Ensure compliance with institutional, sponsor, and regulatory requirements Disseminates and publishes research results in peer-reviewed journals, reports, meetings, workshops, and conferences Assists in the writing of grant proposals May assist in teaching classes May mentor and assist undergraduate and/or graduate students May assist in managing research laboratories Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Demonstrated ability to plan and execute research Knowledge of applicable research methods and analytical procedures Knowledge of research compliance and ethics Knowledge of publishing/reporting requirements Excellent teamwork and communication skills Demonstrated potential for original or collaborative scholarship Scientific writing skills demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications Ability to acquire accurate, reproducible data Critical eye towards consistency, reproducibility, and the scientific method in general Excellent project and time management skills Strong interpersonal and mentoring skills Advocate for safety and ethics in the workplace Ability to communicate findings and effectively work with sponsors and stakeholders Minimum Education & Experience Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a related field Job Level Overview N/A FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $45,000-$55,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Scheduler_JR103409-1": {
      "title": "Scheduler",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Provides scheduling support through the Department of Access Services (DAS). Responsible for the daily coordination of provider assignments and maintaining and updating over 11,000 hours of requests per semester in the DAS staff portal system. The position oversees day-of scheduling for approximately 200+ access service providers, ensuring real-time coverage and rapid response to last-minute changes, cancellation, and absences.   This role serves as the central communication hub for DAS, fielding a high volume of inquiries and dispatches from students, faculty, parents, and staff via phone, email, text, and in-person interactions. It is the main point of contact for departmental concerns, including problem reports and service escalations. The position also manages the DAS on-call system, tracks uncovered assignments throughout the day, and facilitates timely coverage for both academic and non-academic events. The role requires continuous attention to detail, adaptability to frequent changes, the ability to operate under pressure, and a high level of customer service—often requiring extended hours during peak periods. The office operates from 7:00 a.m. to 9:00 p.m., demanding flexibility and a strong commitment to service excellence. This position follows a 10-month schedule, typically from August through May. Major Responsibilities: Scheduling & Data Management: Maintain and update access service requests and assignments in the DAS staff portal (ASDS) system. Verify data accuracy and ensure real-time availability for DAS providers and requesters. Track uncovered assignments and manage daily scheduling, including last-minute changes and on-call assignments. Deliver daily or weekly summaries as needed.  Communication & Customer Service: Serve as the central communication hub for DAS and provide essential support and service across the RIT & NTID communities via diverse communication platforms including email, phone, instant messaging, and in-person engagements. Ensure high-quality interactions, resolution of inquiries, and route issues to appropriate managers. Provide timely updates to coordinators, captionists, and interpreters regarding schedule changes. Student Supervision & Office Operations: Train and support student employees in the DAS scheduling office. Provide back-up support to the Access Services Scheduling Office manager. Supplemental Access Service Coordination: Reconcile freelance and remote billing. Maintain the database for contract service vendors. Coordinate with agencies for last-minute coverage and schedule changes. Departmental Support & Special Projects: Support remote room key sign-outs, parking passes, and other similar processes. Additional responsibilities include: Training and working with student assistants, Coordinating with freelance and remote agencies for service provider coverage and reconciling billing, Managing operational logistics such as remote room key sign-outs, parking passes, and other departmental needs, Maintaining current and accurate information in DAS systems, Facilitates seamless day-to-day activities within the university. Preferred Skills: Ability to evaluate priorities and work with constant interruptions. Handle complaints in a diplomatic, professional manner. Attention to detail. Manage multiple projects simultaneously. Consumer focus. Strong written and signed or spoken communication skills Interact with deaf consumers. Sign language communication skills at the survival plus level or ability and willingness to acquire this proficiency and knowledge of deaf culture.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Addresses both routine and complex, unanticipated issues and inquiries, ensuring timely resolution while maintaining compliance with department and university policies and procedures. Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders on confidential matters Acts as a resource for interpreting practices, processes, and policies, providing clear guidance to others. Represents the department and program in communications with personnel at various levels, managing and safeguarding sensitive and critical information. Advises stakeholders on departmental policies and procedures Assists in the preparation and dissemination of information regarding degree programs, course requirements, curriculum updates, and marketing collateral Manages instructional support tasks such as coordinating course syllabi, administering course evaluations and exams, and responding to student inquiries Provides student services support, including processing tuition waivers, course permits, graduation checks, and tracking student progress Supports the scheduling of courses and assists with academic coordination, ensuring smooth course offerings and scheduling logistics Contributes to student recruitment efforts and accreditation activities such as data analysis, teaching assistant coordination, exam management, and helps coordinate any associated outreach events Assists faculty with grant proposal preparation, tracks grant budgets, and provides guidance on financial processes while responding to inquiries and ensuring policy compliance Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of office management, administrative procedures, and university operations to ensure effective workflow and coordination Knowledge of office software and databases, including tools for scheduling, data analysis, and managing academic records Knowledge of academic program structures, degree requirements, and course curricula to provide accurate information and support to students and faculty Skill in managing and coordinating course schedules, ensuring smooth logistics and alignment with academic calendars Skill in communication and customer service, providing clear and responsive support to students, faculty, and external partners Skill in problem-solving, addressing inquiries, and resolving issues efficiently while maintaining a high level of customer service Ability to coordinate multiple tasks and responsibilities simultaneously, ensuring deadlines are met and operations run smoothly Ability to build positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and external partners, enhancing communication and collaboration Ability to maintain accurate and organized records, ensuring that academic and financial documentation is up-to-date and compliant with university standards Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 3 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $17.90 - $28.60 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Financial-Planning--Analysis----Reporting-Specialist-III_JR103420": {
      "title": "Financial Planning, Analysis, & Reporting Specialist III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nProvide strategic financial leadership and business partnership support for the College of Science, guiding financial planning, budgeting, resource allocation, payroll administration, compliance, and operational decision-making. Support Sponsored Programs Accounting and post-award grant management through oversight of grants, contracts, and cost-share commitments; financial reporting and analysis; compliance monitoring; and collaboration with faculty, staff, and university partners. Serve as a trusted advisor to department leadership and the Dean, helping advance the college's academic, research, and financial priorities through informed decision-making and responsible stewardship of resources   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Designs, prepares, and presents financial information to the leadership team to assist with ongoing management and decision making regarding the college’s finances and operations Maintains analysis and financial forecasting across the organization, including complex compensation-related reconciliations Prepares cost models based on data from general ledger, registrar, student financial services, and fixed assets Completes and evaluates complex reconciliations and analysis of financial accounts, including operating, capital, special, discretionary, start-up, internal grants, and overhead project accounts to ensure transactions are accurate and in compliance with applicable institution policies and other regulatory requirements Develops annual operating budget based on current salary recommendations, current and new academic and operational initiatives, and revenue forecasts Prepares various standard and ad hoc reporting and analysis for management decision-making for multiple stakeholders Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of accounting, finance, and budgeting practices and protocols to ensure accurate financial management and compliance Knowledge of enterprise-wide financial applications and Microsoft Office Skill in synthesizing and analyzing financial data and preparing detailed reports to support decision-making and budgeting activities Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication and customer service Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and exercise professional judgment regarding financial decisions Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 3 - A senior-level role requiring broad understanding of the profession or field of work. Independently leads diverse and often complex assignments, projects, or programs. May act as a mentor and guide less experienced staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $65,900 - $85,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
