    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Gift-Planning-Executive-Director_JR103277": {
      "title": "Gift Planning Executive Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The Gift Planning Executive Director leads the strategy, growth, and execution of RIT’s comprehensive planned and deferred giving program, advancing significant philanthropic investment in support of university priorities. As RIT’s senior subject-matter expert in charitable gift planning, the Executive Director sets program direction, and partners with university and advancement leadership to identify and advance sophisticated gift opportunities.   The Executive Director personally manages a portfolio of high-capacity prospects and donors, developing and executing strategies that result in significant outright, blended, estate, and other complex planned gifts. Working directly with donors and their professional advisors, the Executive Director structures and negotiates charitable arrangements while leading consultation with fundraisers across University Advancement on planned giving strategies and opportunities.   As a senior leader, the Executive Director is accountable for strengthening RIT’s planned giving pipeline and long-term philanthropic support, integrating planned giving across the donor lifecycle, and collaborating with senior leaders, Trustees, volunteers, and colleagues across RIT to advance institutional fundraising priorities. University Advancemen t RIT's University Advancement builds meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, friends, corporations, foundations, and other partners whose engagement and philanthropy advance the university's mission. The division is a collaborative, forward-thinking environment that values trust, accountability, innovation, and shared expertise. Advancement professionals have the opportunity to connect supporters with transformative initiatives that fuel student success, groundbreaking research, experiential learning, and programs that shape the future of technology, health sciences, and creative problem-solving.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Identifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards leadership annual gift and major gift donors and prospects in coordination with faculty, staff, and volunteers Manages a robust portfolio of prospects, creates fundraising strategies, develops relationships with donors, solicits gifts, and coordinates effective donor stewardship Develops an understanding of the educational, research, operational, and financial needs and goals of assigned college Cultivates relationships with alumni, parents, companies, and other friends, and collaborates with the teams in planned giving, principal giving, alumni relations, parent engagement, regional advancement, and corporate and foundation relations to encourage donors to support university initiatives Plans, coordinates, and directs special events for donors and prospects Updates the prospect management database with information related to donor strategies, proposals, contacts, and results Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of cultivating, soliciting, and closing gifts Skill in written and verbal communication Ability to network, establish, and foster working relationships with internal and external stakeholders Ability to manage multiple projects, take initiative, and coordinate follow-up Ability to collect, synthesize, and process information quickly and accurately Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 12 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 5 - An expert-level role functioning as a leading authority in the profession or field of work. Projects or programs of critical, university-wide strategic importance are regularly managed, with substantial consequences of success or failure. Typically responsible for coaching, mentoring, reviewing, and delegating work. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $103,300 - $148,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Director--Army-STEM-Internships---Fellowships_JR103404": {
      "title": "Director, Army STEM Internships & Fellowships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights This Department of War (DoW) grant-funded position leads Army STEM Internships and Fellowships. RIT is the lead organization in the Army STEM Education Consortium (ASEC), a group of academic and non-profit organizations working together to administer a comprehensive portfolio of programming to attract, develop, and mentor the nation’s next-generation STEM workforce. Army STEM offers enrichment experiences, competitions, internships, fellowships, and professional development programs for students of all levels and their teachers. Army STEM Internships and Fellowships enable participants to do paid, hands-on research on real-world problems under the mentorship of Army scientists and engineers at Army-sponsored university labs and U.S. Army Laboratories and Research Centers nation-wide. Army STEM Internships are open to high school and undergraduate students, while graduate students and post-doctoral scientists and engineers are eligible for Army STEM Fellowships. All essential duties and responsibilities of the Director of Army STEM Internships and Fellowships will support Army STEM strategic and operational goals. They will lead the entire Army STEM Internships and Fellowships initiative, with supervision and guidance from RIT’s Army STEM PI. The Director will represent Internships and Fellowships in ASEC and will coordinate and collaborate with the leads of Army STEM Teacher Fellows, the Army Research Office’s (ARO) Internships lead, and the Lab Program Coordinators (LPC) at each participating Army lab. The Director will oversee implementation of the STEM Foundations initiative, a virtual summer program to build STEM identity, and will develop and administer additional curriculums for the Army STEM Learning Management System (LMS). They will manage a staff and an annual budget of $10M+. Some travel required. Open to remote, hybrid, or onsite work arrangement. Preferred qualifications include significant experience in STEM education, mentorship, and career development through graduate and post-doctoral training, experience with Army or DoW STEM, grant and budget management experience, and experience in leading teams to success. PhD preferred.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Designs programs that directly support the university’s strategic, academic, and operational goals. This includes developing project plans, defining objectives and success metrics, coordinating resources, and evaluating outcomes to ensure alignment with institutional priorities Serves as a liaison across departments to align goals, timelines, and deliverables for complex, multi-stakeholder projects. Facilitates communication, resolves conflicts, and ensures coordinated action to enhance program integration and overall institutional impact Develops and oversee program budgets, ensuring responsible financial stewardship. Regularly monitor expenditures and resource allocation. Establishes and tracks performance indicators to evaluate effectiveness, inform decision-making, and support continuous improvement Interprets and applies university policies, accreditation standards, and applicable external regulations to ensure programs operate in full compliance. Anticipates risks and implements practices that maintain institutional accountability and integrity Cultivates strong working relationships with internal departments, faculty, students, and external organizations. Leverages these partnerships to expand program reach, enhance visibility, and create opportunities for collaboration, funding, or innovation Identifies barriers to participation, promoting inclusive practices, and ensuring equitable access and representation. Regularly assess efforts to support a diverse and inclusive campus environment Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of university policies, accreditation standards, and external regulatory requirements Knowledge of budgeting principles and fiscal management. Ability to develop, monitor, and reconcile program budgets, ensuring efficient use of resources and compliance with funding requirements Skill in collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data to assess program performance and support evidence-based decision-making Ability to apply this knowledge to ensure programs operate within legal and institutional frameworks Ability to communicate effectively across diverse groups and foster cooperation among academic, administrative, and external stakeholders Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 8 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Management and People Leadership Level 2 - Manages the operations of a function within a department. Shapes overall success within team or department through planning, coordination, resource allocation, strategy execution, and determination of staffing to ensure achievement of operational results. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Remote Compensation $54,500-$90,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
