    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Building-Facility-Operations-Coordinator--COS-Center-for-Imaging-Science_JR103399": {
      "title": "Building Facility Operations Coordinator, COS Center for Imaging Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The Building Facilities Operations Coordinator keeps the Chester F. Carlson Center for Imaging Science at the Rochester Institute of Technology running smoothly and safely. The 70,000 sq. ft. Carlson building houses 20 laboratories, several classrooms, 40 offices, and a 150-seat auditorium. In addition, this position manages the lab stockroom, supervises student workers and lab GTAs, and ensures equipment is organized, supplied, repaired, and ready for weekly labs. The role oversees critical safety equipment, including fire extinguishers, eyewashes, showers, and exhaust hoods; ensures employees complete required safety training; conducts annual physical inventory; and maintains property accounting procedures, including asset tagging and reporting. They also support A/V needs, equipment improvements, and classroom setup.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Implements preventative maintenance plans for campus housing and facilities, ensuring timely resolution of issues ranging from general repairs to plumbing and painting Executes short-term and long-term projects such as student room upgrades, common area renovations, and special-use space improvements in collaboration with other RIT departments Utilizes work order systems to track maintenance requests, prioritize tasks, and ensure compliance with safety and operational standards; assist maintenance and custodial mechanics as needed Coordinates with campus partners and community stakeholders to assess and address renovation, safety, and operational needs that support a functional and welcoming student environment Oversees day-to-day operations and event scheduling for designated facilities, acting as the primary point of contact for internal and external users and ensuring successful execution of events Acts as the primary facilities contact in the absence of the Associate Director, provide support to the on-call maintenance program, and respond to urgent facility-related incidents—including on-site response when required Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), plumbing, electrical, structural, and general repair systems, including preventative maintenance and facility lifecycle planning Skill in using computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS) or similar platforms to track work orders, manage priorities, and document repairs and preventive maintenance Skill in assessing urgent situations, making sound decisions quickly, and responding to facilities-related emergencies, particularly in a residential or student-centered environment Ability to assess urgent situations, make sound decisions quickly, and respond to facilities-related emergencies, particularly in a residential or student-centered environment Ability to plan, coordinate, and execute small- to medium-scale renovation and improvement projects, including budgeting, scheduling, and collaboration with contractors and campus partners Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 3 years of related experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $19.65 - $31.45 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Sr-Marketing---Promotions-Coordinator--Saunders-College-of-Business_JR103400-1": {
      "title": "Sr Marketing & Promotions Coordinator, Saunders College of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The Senior Marketing & Promotions Coordinator is an integral member of the Marketing and Communication Department at Saunders College of Business at RIT. The position reports directly to the director of marketing and communications. This is an on campus position although there are currently flexible work options that do allow some remote work days.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Supports the day-to-day operations of the department through administrative tasks including scheduling, sending/updating calendar invites and conference calls, preparing meeting and presentation materials, and providing customer service Maintains department websites and updates website content as needed Coordinates the printing of publications and marketing materials using on-and off-campus vendors Monitors, tracks, and assesses marketing success, through data collection and analysis Performs market research to support campaigns, projects, and initiatives Ensures the proper documentation, organization, and maintenance of project documents and files Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of administrative procedures and practices Knowledge of communications and marketing strategies Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail Ability to perform quantitative and qualitative data analysis and use data to influence decision making Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 4 - Advanced or lead role with deep subject matter expertise and/or functions as a formal or informal team lead. Leads challenging and non-routine tasks, assignments, and projects, often coordinating across teams and developing new methods or techniques. Mentors less experienced staff and reviews or delegates work. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $23.80-$30.00 per hour Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
