    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Computational-Linguistics-Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-in_JR103353": {
      "title": "Computational Linguistics Tenure-Track Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Psychology and Cognitive Science at the Rochester Institute of Technology invites applications for a full-time, 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Computational Linguistics, beginning in August 2027. Candidates are expected to have an earned doctoral degree (in hand by August 2027) in Linguistics, Computational Linguistics, or a related field. The position additionally offers an affiliation with the Department of Modern Languages and Cultures in the School of Languages, Humanities, and Social Sciences. Successful candidates should demonstrate computational expertise, strong research talent, and initiative in grant writing. Candidates should also have a plan for excellence in teaching and student mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applicants must be able to teach our courses in language technology and large language models, natural language processing, and/or computational speech processing. In addition, applicants should be able to teach foundational linguistics from a cross-linguistic perspective, as well as courses in at least one additional linguistics, artificial intelligence, or cognitive science subfield. Proficiency in an additional language other than English is preferred, and we welcome research or teaching experience involving language learning. The position requires a commitment to teaching and mentoring, active research and publication, and a strong potential to attract external funding. Research and teaching are priorities for faculty at RIT, and all faculty are expected to mentor graduate and undergraduate students through advising, research, and in-class experiences. The computational linguistics-related programs at RIT serve a rapidly expanding student population at a technical university. We are looking for a faculty colleague who can also contribute to the interdisciplinary M.S. program in Artificial Intelligence and the Ph.D. program in Cognitive Science. Our coursework is also offered to B.S. in Artificial Intelligence majors. In addition, RIT provides many opportunities for collaborative research across the institute in areas such as linguistics of sign languages and languages other than English, artificial intelligence, human-centered computing, and cybersecurity. RIT faculty have access to extensive research computing resources.   REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: ●      Ph.D. (in hand by August 2027) in Linguistics, Computational Linguistics, or a related field. ●      Have demonstrated ability to conduct independent research in computational linguistics.  ●      Demonstrate potential for external research grant attainment. ●      Have consistently and recently published in computational linguistics. ●      Demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching language technology, natural language processing, and/or computational speech processing. ●      Demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching foundational linguistics from a cross-linguistic perspective, and courses in at least one more linguistics, artificial intelligence, or cognitive science subfield. ●      Demonstrate potential for excellence in supervising graduate and undergraduate student research. ●      Show a career trajectory that emphasizes a balance between research and teaching. Priority application deadline: November 15, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Cecilia Alm, at < coagla@rit.edu > with any questions. Faculty Tenure, Rank, Discipline JC_1414 - Assistant Professor, Psychology Work Location Hybrid Compensation $80,000-$90,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Anticipated Start Date August 16, 2027 Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Assistant-Professor-Computer-Engineering_JR103351": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRIT’s Department of Computer Engineering invites applications from highly motivated individuals looking to join a vibrant community of teacher-scholars as a tenure-track faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor. Successful candidates are expected to build a strong externally-funded research program, advise Ph.D. and master's students, develop and teach undergraduate and graduate classes, advise undergraduate researchers and design teams, and work collaboratively to advance the goals of the department.  We are currently seeking candidates with research expertise in one or more of the following areas: Machine Learning and Edge AI, Heterogeneous Computing, Networking and IoT, Quantum Computing. We are seeking an individual who has the ability and interest in contributing to a community committed to student-centeredness; professional development and scholarship; integrity and ethics; respect, innovation and flexibility; and teamwork and collaboration. Select to view links to RIT’s core values , honor code , and commitment to community statement. Salary Range: $100,000 – $130,000   THE COLLEGE/ DEPARTMENT: The Computer Engineering Department is one of s ix academic departments in the Kate Gleason College of Engineering.  Th e Kate Gleason College of Engineering | RIT offers bachelor’s and master’s in biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, computer engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and microelectronics engineering as well as four Ph.D. degrees in biomedical and chemical engineering, electrical and computer engineering, mechanical and industrial engineering, and microsystems engineering and additional master’s programs in engineering management and leadership.  Serving over 2600 undergraduates and 400 graduate students, the college is committed to growing its research profile while maintaining a strong commitment to undergraduate education.  Major research themes include advanced manufacturing; biomedical and healthcare engineering; artificial intelligence and machine learning; cyber-physical systems; micro- and nanoscale systems devices and materials; energy and environment; and data analysis modeling and simulation. Hallmarks of the undergraduate experience include one full year of cooperative education, an innovative multidisciplinary senior design program, and an impressive variety of well-supported student teams and clubs.  The Computer Engineering Department has about four hundred and fifty undergraduates, one hundred graduate students, and eighteen faculty and staff.  The department is known for its outstanding curricula, career-oriented education, collaborative research and state-of-the-art laboratories and computing facilities. Faculty members are actively engaged in research, innovative teaching, and partnerships with industry, and participate in the Electrical and Computer Engineering Ph.D. and cross-disciplinary Ph.D. programs in Computing and Information Sciences, Microsystems Engineering, and Imaging Science. For more information, visit https://www.rit.edu/kgcoe/computerengineering/ . THE UNIVERSITY AND ROCHESTER COMMUNITY: Rochester Institute of Technology is home to leading creators, entrepreneurs, innovators, and researchers. The university enrolls 16,868 undergraduates and 2,904 graduate students in more than 200 programs, and across nine academic colleges, five international campuses, as well as other degree-granting units, placing it among some of the largest private universities in the U.S. RIT is internationally recognized and ranked for academic leadership in business, computing, engineering, imaging science, liberal arts, sustainability, and fine and applied arts. RIT is also home to the National Technical Institute for the Deaf, the world’s first and largest technological college for deaf and hard-of-hearing students. With more than 900 students from around the world, NTID offers unparalleled support services for deaf and hard-of-hearing students. RIT’s cooperative education program is one of the oldest and largest in the nation. The university revised its 2025 strategic plan, Greatness Through Difference, in the fall of 2018. The plan leverages RIT’s unique history with a renewed focus on using the interdisciplinary power of technology, the arts, and design to shape the future and the world. In 2019, RIT moved into the high research activity institution or “R2” category under the updated Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Learning, ranking it among the top six percent of colleges and universities in the nation for research activity. U.S. News and World Report ( USNWR ) now ranks RIT No. 105 in its “National Universities” category, and No. 54 and No. 63 for Best Undergraduate and Graduate Engineering Programs, respectively. The publication also ranks RIT No. 11 in the U.S. for co-op or internship programs, No. 48 among best-value schools, and No. 41 among most innovative. Sponsored research awards totaled $92 million in the fiscal year 2022, up from $78 million in 2018. Today, RIT counts nearly 140,000 alumni around the world. Its endowment is currently valued at $1.257 billion, and the university benefits from sound financial management. Always on the cutting edge, RIT’s educational programs continue to evolve to meet the needs of today’s students. Building on its legacy of excellence across STEM and the arts and its commitment to developing creative thinkers, RIT launched the Performing Arts Scholars program in 2019. In the fall of 2022, 482 first-year students accepted scholarships to join this program, regardless of major, bringing the total number of PA Scholars to 1,400. In support of this programming, RIT is unveiling the Student Hall for Exploration and Development (SHED) in the fall of 2023, with major facilities for the performing arts, and new classrooms, surrounding an enormous multi-story core of maker spaces. RIT has also launched a series of very successful Combined Accelerated Bachelor’s/Master’s Degree (CAB-M) programs, which attracted about 750 students in the fall of 2022. In addition, RIT is developing a large suite of online programs with an emphasis on upskilling for adult learners through its offerings at RIT Certified. QUALIFICATIONS:   REQUIRED: ·         Doctorate in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or closely related field Ability and commitment to effectively teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students  Record of disseminating scholarly research in refereed (peer-reviewed) publications   Demonstrated evidence of experience or potential to establish an independent externally-sponsored research program Expertise in the areas of Edge AI, Heterogeneous Computing, Networking and IoT, and/or Quantum Computing. Excellent communication skills Ability to contribute in meaningful ways to the university’s continuing commitment to cultural diversity, pluralism and individual differences. Interest in working in a collaborative, collegial environment HOW TO APPLY:   Candidates may apply online at http://careers.rit.edu select Faculty Positions, then Keyword Search.  Please upload the following documents to complete the application:     ·         Cover letter ·         Curriculum Vita ·         Research Statement ·         Statement of Teaching Philosophy ·         List of three references Questions for the search committee should be sent to Dr. Cory Merkel at cemeec@rit.edu.   A review of applications will begin by January 15, 2027 and continue until a suitable candidate is found.   Faculty Tenure, Rank, Discipline JC_1381 - Assistant Professor, Computer Engineering Work Location On Campus Compensation $100,000-$130,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Anticipated Start Date July 01, 2027 Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Residence-Coordinator_JR103432": {
      "title": "Residence Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Join a dedicated team committed to creating a welcoming, inclusive, and engaging residential experience for RIT students. Residence Coordinators play a vital role in fostering student success by supporting residential communities, advising student leaders, responding to student concerns, and promoting personal growth and belonging within the residence halls. This is an exciting opportunity for a student-centered professional who is passionate about leadership development, community building, and supporting college students through their residential experience. Residence Coordinators serve as key members of the Residence Life team, working collaboratively with students, families, faculty, and campus partners to create safe, vibrant, and inclusive living-learning environments. Key responsibilities include supervising and developing Resident Advisors, managing residential operations, addressing student conduct and behavioral concerns, supporting crisis response efforts, implementing educational and community-building initiatives, and contributing to departmental projects that enhance the student experience. Our Residence Coordinator roles are full-time, live-in positions that include year-round housing. Residence Coordinators are expected to participate in an on-call rotation and provide after-hours support as needed to address student emergencies and community concerns. Residence Life / Student Life Residence Life is committed to creating residential communities where students feel connected, supported, and empowered to thrive academically, socially, and personally. Through intentional community engagement, leadership development, educational programming, and student support services, Residence Life helps students build meaningful relationships and develop skills that contribute to lifelong success. As part of the Division of Student Affairs, Residence Life partners closely with campus departments to promote student well-being, foster belonging, and create residential environments that support learning both inside and outside the classroom. Our team values collaboration, inclusivity, student development, and continuous improvement in service of RIT's diverse student population. What You'll Do Supervise, train, mentor, and evaluate a team of Resident Advisors and student leaders. Foster inclusive, welcoming, and supportive residential communities. Respond to student concerns, crisis situations, and emergency incidents. Address student conduct matters and facilitate educational interventions. Develop and implement programs that support student engagement, leadership development, and community building. Advise student groups and collaborate with campus partners to support student success initiatives. Participate in an on-call rotation and provide after-hours support for residential communities.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Manages a university residential community including the selection, training and supervision of undergraduate and graduate students assigned to the residence Provides leadership and guidance for business operation processes such as facilities opening and closing procedures, facilities management, and related areas Develops and implements educational and cultural programs, services, and activities in the residential community, with a focus on the principles of community development, student engagement, wellness, diversity, inclusion, and retention Ensures budgeting, personnel matters, and reporting are managed in accordance with university, state, and federal guidelines, regulations, procedures, and policies Oversees the response to, resolution of, and decision-making for matters of significance such as emergency housing, involvement of other offices, parental contact, etc Meets with students to resolve complex issues, makes referrals, and conducts follow-up as needed in areas including, but not limited to: social skill development, personal safety, conflict resolution, understanding of university policy and procedures, and academic success Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of student development theories and practices Knowledge of crisis management/conflict resolution Skill in advising and coaching Skill in using technology and systems to support administrative, operation and program functions Ability to manage and maintain confidential and private information; use confidential, sensitive and/or private records and information, and protect information appropriately Ability to establish, build and maintain effective working relationships based on respect, empathy and honesty with diverse groups and individuals Minimum Education & Experience Master's degree in related field 1 year of relevant experience Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 2 - A fully functional role requiring established knowledge of the profession or field of work. Responsible for completing substantive assignments and projects. Problems are varied and non-routine, and resolution requires exercising judgment, analysis, advisement, creativity, and understanding broader sets of issues. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $50,000 - $60,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Assistant-Professor--Sustainability_JR103339": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sustainability",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Sustainability Department at the Rochester Institute of Technology (Rochester, NY) invites applications for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Sustainability.    The successful applicant will demonstrate the potential to become a leading expert in sustainability research that is distinct from but complementary to research by our current core faculty. We particularly seek candidates whose research is collaborative and applies systems approaches (including but not limited to applied data science, industrial ecology, multi-criteria decision analysis, techno-economic analysis, and quantitative behavioral analysis) to addressing sustainability challenges in areas such as circular economy, sustainable manufacturing, sustainable materials management, food systems/organic waste, energy systems, and transportation systems.   The faculty member will build an externally funded research program to support multiple Ph.D. students and conduct research that is responsive to societal needs and that leads to peer-reviewed, scholarly publications as well as the communication or translation of research outcomes to realize broader impacts.   The faculty member will teach two graduate-level courses each year to support the MS and PhD programs. Course information can be found at https://www.rit.edu/study/sustainability-phd#curriculum . Teaching responsibilities also include recruiting, mentoring, and advising a group of Ph.D. and M.S. students.   The faculty member will contribute to university service by participating on a limited number of department and institute committees and to professional service by engaging with external community groups and/or scholarly organizations.   We seek an individual who has the ability and interest in contributing to a community committed to student-centeredness; professional development and scholarship; integrity and ethics; respect, innovation and flexibility; and teamwork and collaboration. Select to view links to RIT’s core values , honor code , and commitment to community statement .   The faculty appointment and listed salary are for a 9-month academic year appointment (salary paid out over 12 months), with the opportunity to augment academic year salary in the summer through external research grants.   THE DEPARTMENT The successful applicant will join the Sustainability Department, which offers M.S. in Sustainable Systems and Ph.D. in Sustainability degrees.The department recognizes and is committed to the value of a diverse graduate student community, with strong recruitment and enrollment of female and underrepresented students. Sustainability faculty typically support research groups of about 4-6 Ph.D. students, 1-2 M.S. students (thesis track), and sometimes a postdoctoral scholar. Faculty also provide academic advising to 2-3 M.S. students on the capstone track. Sustainability faculty collaborate with researchers across RIT and with organizations locally, nationally, and internationally to create solutions to complex sustainability challenges. The department is housed in the LEED platinum-certified Sustainability Hall, a $38 million, 84,000 ft2 facility dedicated to the GIS academic mission.  The building serves as a center for sustainability research, technology transfer, education and outreach, and provides a state-of-the-art showcase for green construction and design. Additional information can be found at https://www.rit.edu/study/sustainability-phd .   THE UNIVERSITY AND ROCHESTER COMMUNITY Founded in 1829, Rochester Institute of Technology is a diverse and collaborative community of engaged, socially conscious, and intellectually curious minds. Through creativity and innovation, and an intentional blending of technology, the arts and design, we provide exceptional individuals with a wide range of academic opportunities, including a leading research program and an internationally recognized education for deaf and hard-of-hearing students. Beyond our main campus in Rochester, New York, RIT has international campuses in China, Croatia, Dubai, and Kosovo. And with more than 19,000 students and more than 125,000 graduates from all 50 states and over 100 nations, RIT is driving progress in industries and communities around the world. Find out more at www.rit.edu .   REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Assistant Professor Rank: Ph.D. by August 2027. A strong collaborative scholarly research agenda that will apply a systems approach to sustainability and lead to peer-reviewed scholarly publications and broader societal impacts. Potential to secure external funding resources to support multiple PhD students. Potential to advise graduate students and excel at graduate-level teaching in GIS core and elective courses. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to contribute in meaningful ways to the college’s continuing commitment to cultural diversity, pluralism, and individual differences. Potential to develop a research trajectory that will complement but not significantly overlap the research of current GIS faculty. Potential to build collaborations within RIT and/or with external manufacturing firms, government agencies, national labs, and/or domestic or international research universities.   Please submit the following materials: Cover letter addressing listed qualifications; Curriculum vita; Research statement focusing on future plans for research, external funding, publication, and translation of research for broader impacts; Teaching statement that presents future plans and qualifications for teaching specific GIS core and elective courses of interest; Names and contact information of three references the committee can contact.   Please send any questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Callie Babbitt at cwgis@rit.edu or to the Department Head Dr. Amit Batabyal at aabgsh@rit.edu The review of applications will begin January 18, 2027 and continue until acceptable candidates have been identified.  HOW TO APPLY: Apply online at RIT Careers; go to Job Category, and select Faculty (Regular) to view current openings. Please submit your application and upload the following attachments: Cover letter addressing listed qualifications; Curriculum vita; Research statement focusing on future plans for research, external funding, publication, and translation of research for broader impacts; Teaching statement that presents future plans and qualifications for teaching specific GIS core and elective courses of interest; Names and contact information of three references the committee can contact.   Please send any questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Callie Babbitt at cwgis@rit.edu or to the Department Head Dr. Amit Batabyal at aabgsh@rit.edu   The review of applications will begin January 18, 2027 and continue until acceptable candidates have been identified.  Faculty Tenure, Rank, Discipline JC_1418 - Assistant Professor, Sustainability Work Location On Campus Compensation $86,000-$96,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Anticipated Start Date August 15, 2027 Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Multimedia-Design-Coordinator_JR103329": {
      "title": "Multimedia Design Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Highlights The Multimedia Design Coordinator supports University Advancement’s marketing and donor relations efforts by creating engaging visual content across print and digital platforms. Working closely with the Multimedia Designer and the Marketing & Donor Relations team, this role helps develop marketing materials that bring University Advancement’s stories, initiatives, and impact to life. This part-time position (approximately 20 hours per week) offers a flexible opportunity for an emerging designer to gain hands-on experience while contributing to meaningful projects that engage alumni, donors, parents, and friends of RIT. The role provides exposure to the full creative process, from concept development and design through production and quality review, while collaborating with colleagues and cross-functional partners across the university. As a Multimedia Design Coordinator, you will support the conceptualization, design, and production of visual assets across a variety of print and digital mediums, helping advance the marketing, communication, and educational initiatives of RIT University Advancement. This is an ideal opportunity for a creative professional looking to strengthen their design skills, build a diverse portfolio, and make a meaningful impact in a collaborative higher education environment. As a Multimedia Design Coordinator, you will support the conceptualization, design, and production of visual assets across various mediums—supporting various marketing and educational initiatives of RIT University Advancement.  Job Responsibilities: Graphic Design and Layout: Create visually appealing designs for marketing materials. Apply principles of layout, typography, and color theory to deliver designs that engage and target audiences.  Design Support: Assist in the development and execution of creative concepts for print and digital projects. Contribute ideas and solutions that align with divisional objectives and brand guidelines.  Production and File Preparation: Prepare design files for production, ensuring accuracy, consistency, and adherence to technical specifications.  Project Coordination and Communication: Assist in project coordination and communication, including scheduling meetings, organizing files, and managing project timelines. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure the successful execution of creative projects.  Quality Assurance and Revision: Assist in the review and revision of design deliverables to ensure accuracy, quality, and consistency. Incorporate feedback from clients and team members to refine designs and improve overall project outcomes.  Creative Research, Inspiration, and Professional Development: Stay abreast of design trends, emerging technologies, and best practices in graphic design and digital media. Seek out learning opportunities and skill development activities to enhance your design skills and expand your knowledge of design principles, software tools, and industry trends.  Other duties as assigned.   Required skills: Adobe Creative Suite, Adobe InDesign, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Illustrator, Microsoft Office Suite, Brand Guidelines, File Organization, File Preparation, Print Design, Digital Design University Advancement | Alumni & Constituent Engagement University Advancement fosters meaningful connections between RIT and its alumni, donors, parents, friends, and community partners. Within University Advancement, the Alumni & Constituent Engagement team develops programs, events, communications, and volunteer opportunities that strengthen lifelong relationships with the university and inspire engagement with the RIT community. Through collaboration, service, and relationship-building, the team supports RIT's mission and helps create lasting impact for students, alumni, and the university.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Supports multimedia project coordination, working closely with other designers and departments to ensure project requirements are met Drafts initial designs for multimedia content, including digital graphics, videos, and interactive media, aligning with the university’s visual identity Utilizes and stays current with the latest design technologies and software to produce high-quality, innovative content Helps maintain a consistent visual identity across all media outputs, aligning with the university's design standards Assists in managing project timelines and budgets, ensuring deliverables are completed on schedule and within specified financial parameters Works alongside other design and marketing professionals to brainstorm, critique, and refine multimedia content that meets strategic objectives Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of graphic design principles, tools, and applications Knowledge of website design and development Ability to design, prepare, and edit creative content directed at specific audiences using design requirements, parameters, timeline, and budget Skill in multi-tasking, project management, prioritization, and organization Skill in oral and written communication, with the Ability to present design ideas and concepts clearly to business partners, technical staff, and end users, ensuring a shared understanding across diverse stakeholders Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field No experience required Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $19.65 - $31.45 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Director--Digital-Experience-and-Strategy-for-Enrollment-Management_JR103317": {
      "title": "Director, Digital Experience and Strategy for Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Each year, over one million prospective and current students, school counselors, parents, and other key stakeholders visit and access Enrollment Management digital platforms, obtaining information, interacting with the campus community, scheduling visits, registering for events, requesting information, and applying for admission. The divisional digital platforms (websites, social, digital screens, advertisements, experiential tools) directly influence the enrollment of approximately 5,000 new students annually and provide financial aid information and services to more than 12,000 students.   The Director, Digital Experience and Strategy leads and manages all digital projects focused on relationship building between RIT and the prospective student marketplace by aligning digital architecture, content, and experiences with the strategic needs of the prospective student market for admissions, and the prospect and current student market for financial aid. On a day-to-day basis, this position oversees the strategic development and maintenance of digital content and user experiences aimed at making relationship-building simple, experiential, informative, and highly effective. This includes comprehensive management of the admissions and financial aid domains of the rit.edu site, all related content located throughout rit.edu, social media content, and other digital content management. This role also leads the implementation and strategic utilization of generative AI, chat bots, personalized portals, and other advanced digital applications to improve human connectivity and engagement.   The position directly reports to the Associate Vice President for Enrollment Marketing and Global Strategic Initiatives. The Director is a critical collaborative partner with the entire Enrollment Management division for new initiatives, supports university-wide efforts in maintaining and continuously improving the rit.edu digital presence, and leads the adoption of digital project management and collaboration tools. The position is integral to ensuring that the division’s web and overall digital media presence is easy to navigate, delivers exceptional service experiences while optimizing resource allocation and reducing costs, and ultimately enhances the division's efficiency and effectiveness. This position requires a sophisticated combination of digital strategy, user experience (UX) and web strategy, technical skills, project management, analytical skills, team leadership, and high-level customer service. Key responsibilities include: Strategic Digital Leadership: Proven ability to develop and execute long-term digital strategies that drive results, align with institutional goals, and adapt to a dynamic environment; strong business acumen and strategic thinking. Comprehensive User Experience (UX) and Web Strategy: Deep expertise in user-centered design principles, research methodologies, and optimizing digital journeys; advanced knowledge of web design, usability, accessibility (ADA compliance), mobile optimization, responsive design, and visual communication. Advanced Web and Technical Proficiency: Mastery of modern standards-based web technologies, including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, front-end frameworks; specific expertise with Drupal CMS. Data-Driven Optimization and Analytics: Demonstrated ability to analyze performance metrics, interpret data for actionable insights, and drive data-informed decisions utilizing tools such as Google Analytics, CrazyEgg, Siteimprove, and BrightEdge SEO; proven experience in Conversion Rate Optimization (CRO) and A/B testing. Digital Engagement and CRM Integration: Superb understanding of social media platforms and institution-wide digital content and advertising strategies; experience managing digital customer journeys, specifically with Slate Technolution CRM. Project, Vendor, and Operational Management: Demonstrated leadership in digital project management, including leading adoption of project management/collaboration tools; experience overseeing digital initiatives and effectively managing external digital vendors. Exceptional Communication and Cross-functional Collaboration: Proven ability to translate complex technical concepts and requirements into clear business solutions for non-technical stakeholders; high-level internal customer service skills. Crisis Management and Availability: Experience in crisis communication strategies leveraging digital platforms; availability for off-hour crisis support. Preferred education, experience or specialized skills:   Bachelors required/Master’s preferred in Web/Graphic Design, User Experience Design, Digital Marketing, Computer Science, Information Technology, or other related fields. Experience in higher education or student recruitment preferred Experience leading or building a digital team in a growing or evolving organization. Proactive experience monitoring industry trends, technologies, and standards, with the ability to research, recommend, and apply new technologies as they emerge to drive innovation. Knowledge of broader customer experience (CX) strategies and tools, and familiarity with additional marketing automation platforms beyond core CRM integration. Exceptional troubleshooting skills.     Essential Duties & Responsibilities Designs, implements, and assesses the effectiveness of the university marketing and communications strategy. Gathers and prioritizes objectives, sets course of action, and deploys necessary resources Conceptualizes and executes multi-channel campaigns to ensure the alignment of communications and messaging across all traditional and non-traditional channels Builds and manages long-term relationships among faculty, staff, and alumni. Provides expert consultation and recommends marketing and communication strategies Leads, supervises, and mentors professional and paraprofessional staff. Assigns and prioritizes work and provides performance evaluations Administers, oversees, and monitors budget planning and expenditures Participates as a key member of the division. Collaborates with team members and provides support for department, division, and university initiatives Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of communications, public relations, marketing, branding, graphic design, and social media Ability to write, proofread, and edit clear, concise, persuasive, and grammatically correct communications Ability to translate vision, strategic direction, and long-term goals into communications tasks and projects Ability to motivate, guide, and coach others to achieve department and university vision and goals Skill in multi-tasking, project management, prioritization, and organization Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 8 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Management and People Leadership Level 3 - Heads a department, multiple smaller functions with a department, or a specialized function with institution-wide span. Integrates strategic thinking to drive cross functional initiatives to optimize efficiency, performance, and innovation. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Remote Compensation $81,600-$90,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Senior-SAFE-Lab-Cybersecurity-Engineer_JR103361": {
      "title": "Senior SAFE Lab Cybersecurity Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The Senior SAFE Lab Cybersecurity Engineer leads offensive security assessments and adversary-emulation campaigns for corporate clients. They produce reports and provide briefings to clients. They are responsible for supervising teams of student employees and adjunct consultants.   The Senior Cyber SAFE Engineer is the Cyber Range and Training Center's principal offensive security practitioner and the technical author of the adversary activity on which the Center's commercial, academic, and research programs depend. Realistic, instrumented, repeatable adversary emulation is the core product of the Center's fee-for-service training and assessment work.   Key responsibilities include: leads client-facing security testing and evaluation in the SAFE Lab: penetration testing and ethical hacking of enterprise, government, military, and cyber-physical environments, and the translation of those findings into written reports and briefings that non-technical executives and technical practitioners can both act on. converts assessment findings and current threat intelligence into staged, observable attack campaigns that drive the Center's immersive exercises, competitions, and client engagements -- and ensures that those campaigns generate the telemetry participants must be able to find, in the tools and formats those participants actually use.   The Senior SAFE Lab Cybersecurity Engineer serves as exercise control during live delivery, adapting scenario tempo and injects in real time while paying clients are in the room, and is accountable for the technical integrity of engagements that carry contractual delivery obligations. The position also leads teams of student employees and industry-expert adjunct consultants and is expected to document its work to a standard that allows another qualified engineer to reproduce any engagement independently. This position reports to the Director of the Cyber Range and Training Center within RIT's ESL Global Cybersecurity Institute and is expected to lead engagements independently with low-touch oversight.      Preferred experience: A minimum of 5 years of professional experience in offensive security, including penetration testing, red teaming, or adversary emulation against production or production-representative environments. A minimum of 2 years of experience designing or executing adversary emulation, red team, purple team, or cyber exercise scenarios in which the activity was instrumented and observed by a defending audience. At least 3 years of client-facing consulting experience, including scoping, statement-of-work input, and level-of-effort estimation for fee-for-service engagements. Demonstrated experience leading engagements and directing the work of other technical contributors. Demonstrated experience delivering written assessment reports and verbal briefings directly to paying or sponsoring clients. Experience designing and deploying system/network environments using Openstack and infrastructure-as-code (ansible/terraform/etc). Experience designing or delivering cyber exercises, wargames, tabletop-to-technical hybrids, or competition infrastructure for external audiences. Detection engineering experience: authoring SIEM correlation content, EDR detections, or purple-team validation of detective controls. Experience with Splunk Enterprise Security, CrowdStrike, or comparable commercial detection stacks in a client-aligned configuration. Experience applying AI and large language model tooling to offensive security or exercise workflows — including agentic tooling and Model Context Protocol integrations — together with sound judgment regarding validation, data handling, and disclosure. Experience evaluating AI-enabled security products under realistic adversarial conditions and reporting evidence-based adoption guidance. Experience with cloud and identity attack paths in Azure/Entra ID, AWS, or Google Cloud. Experience with operational technology, ICS/SCADA, or energy-grid networks, devices, and protocols. Experience creating models or digital twins of tested networks and deploying them using infrastructure as code such as Ansible or Terraform, or simulation platforms such as Unreal Engine or MATLAB Simulink. At least two years of experience managing or maintaining enterprise IT infrastructure (servers, storage, network, or security). Experience mentoring students or junior engineers, and prior involvement in academic or government research projects related to cybersecurity. Certifications such as CISSP, GCIH, GCFA, or PMP. Existing security clearance or the ability to obtain one. Dedication to learning and advancing your skills.   Preferred Skills Deep expertise in penetration testing tools and methodologies, with a current certification such as OSCP, OSEP, GPEN, GXPN, CRTO, or equivalent, or the ability to obtain one within six months of hire. Demonstrated ability to compromise and operate within Windows Active Directory environments, including credential attacks, Kerberos abuse, delegation, trust relationships, and domain persistence. Working command of the MITRE ATT&CK framework and the ability to design attack chains that map to specific techniques and defined learning objectives. Hands-on experience with command-and-control and adversary emulation frameworks such as Cobalt Strike, Sliver, Mythic, Havoc, Caldera, or Atomic Red Team, and the judgment to operate them safely in isolated environments. Practical understanding of how offensive activity appears in defensive telemetry, and the ability to validate that an emulated attack produces the intended, discoverable evidence. Working proficiency with SIEM and log platforms — Splunk and Wazuh in particular — including search authoring, data onboarding, field extraction, and log formatting. Proficiency administering Windows and Linux systems and enterprise networking sufficient to build, segment, and troubleshoot isolated exercise environments. Scripting and automation ability in Python, PowerShell, and Bash, and working familiarity with version control and infrastructure-as-code practice. Ability to write clearly for both executive and deeply technical audiences, and to deliver briefings and hotwashes with composure under scrutiny. Ability to maintain accurate documentation to a standard that allows another qualified engineer to reproduce the work independently. Sound professional judgment regarding authorization boundaries, rules of engagement, safety of destructive techniques, client data handling, and export-control obligations. Ability to remain composed and effective while diagnosing technical faults during live, high-visibility, revenue-bearing engagements. Familiarity with regulations and standards relevant to cybersecurity and privacy. Ability to work within a team setting and to direct the work of students and adjunct consultants. Availability for evening, weekend, and consecutive multi-day work in support of exercise schedules, and for occasional travel.     Essential Duties & Responsibilities Conducts vulnerability scanning and penetration testing Investigates services and application security. Performs security comparative review, security risk assessment, and security validation Performs operational duties during security incident responses, troubleshoots and performs root cause analysis for security solutions Analyzes, designs, and installs complex enterprise security solutions and frameworks Designs security solutions architecture, selects tools and partners, and configures and manages capacity, changes, documentation, and reporting Contributes to the documentation of security processes and procedures Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of security architecture principles and best practices for system and network protection Knowledge of advanced cybersecurity tools, such as firewalls and intrusion prevention systems Skill in deploying and configuring cybersecurity tools and technologies to mitigate risks Skill in designing and implementing security measures to protect IT infrastructure and sensitive data Ability to lead complex technical projects Ability to analyze complex security threats and develop proactive solutions to prevent breaches Ability to troubleshoot and resolve advanced security incidents with minimal supervision Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of related experience Equivalent combination of experience & education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 3 - A senior-level role requiring broad understanding of the profession or field of work. Independently leads diverse and often complex assignments, projects, or programs. May act as a mentor and guide less experienced staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $81,600-$100,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Assistant-Professor--Mechanical-Engineering-Multiple-Openings_JR103349": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering-Multiple Openings",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRIT’s Department of Mechanical Engineering invites applications for three tenure-track Assistant Professor positions. We seek highly motivated individuals who are committed to excellence in both research and teaching and are eager to contribute to a vibrant academic community. We are specifically looking for candidates in each of the three following broad areas: Digital Twins in Mechanical Engineering and Design . Interests include but are not limited to: physics-informed and hybrid physics-ML modeling; digital twins for engineering design and manufacturing, including AI-assisted and generative design, additive manufacturing, and product lifecycle; and uncertainty quantification, verification and validation, and real-time model updating for decision-ready digital twins. Controls, Systems, and Sensors Interests include but are not limited to: dynamics and control of robotic and autonomous systems; cyber-physical systems, including estimation, learning-based control, and system integration; and sensors and sensor systems, spanning physical, bio-, and electrochemical sensors, including printed, flexible, and wearable devices. Composite Materials in Aerospace Applications Interests include but are not limited to: AI-enabled design and discovery of composite materials; autonomous/intelligent manufacturing of composites; composite materials for extreme environments; and damage prediction and structural health monitoring. Candidates should only apply to one position that best aligns with their expertise and should clearly indicate the position in their cover letter. Successful candidates are expected to build and sustain a strong externally funded research program, advise Ph.D. and master's students, develop and teach undergraduate and graduate classes, advise undergraduate researchers and design teams, and work collaboratively to advance the department's goals. We are seeking individuals who are able and interested in contributing to a community committed to student-centeredness; professional development and scholarship; integrity and ethics; respect; innovation and flexibility; and teamwork and collaboration. Select to view links to RIT’s core values , honor code . Questions for the search committee should be directed to Dr. Xudong Zheng ( xxzeme@rit.edu ). For full consideration, please submit your application by Friday, November 6, 2026 . Department/College Description: With over 1000 undergraduate and graduate students, the Mechanical Engineering Department is the largest of the six academic departments in the Kate Gleason College of Engineering.  It is currently experiencing significant growth, with enrollment on track to increase by 30% in the upcoming years. The department currently includes 23 tenured and tenure-track faculty, 15 lecturers, and 11 staff members.  The department offers a BS in Mechanical Engineering with options in automotive engineering, aerospace engineering, energy and the environment, and bioengineering and an accelerated BS-ME/MS program.  Graduate programs include an MS and ME in Mechanical Engineering and a PhD in Mechanical and Industrial Engineering.  Faculty research is supported by a wide range of core facilities across campus including a fully staffed mechanical engineering machine shop providing machining, fabrication, design, and manufacturing services. The University houses 17 Research Centers and Institutes , including the AMPrint Center for Additive Manufacturing and Multifunctional Printing , a NY State Center for Advanced Technology , the Battery Prototyping and Testing Center , the Center for Human-aware AI, the NanoPower Research Laboratories, Personalized Healthcare Technology, and the Center for Innovation in Manufacturing and Sustainability , as well as many others. Additional resources include the high-performance computing cluster through RIT Research Computing and the Semiconductor Nanofabrication Laboratory with state-of-the-art cleanroom facilities. The Kate Gleason College of Engineering | RIT offers bachelor’s and master’s in biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, computer engineering, electrical engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, and microelectronics engineering as well as four Ph.D. degrees in biomedical and chemical engineering, electrical and computer engineering, mechanical and industrial Engineering, and microsystems engineering and additional master’s programs in engineering management and leadership.  Serving over 2600 undergraduates and 400 graduate students, the college is committed to growing its research profile while maintaining a strong commitment to undergraduate education.  Major research themes include advanced manufacturing; biomedical and healthcare engineering; artificial intelligence and machine learning; cyber-physical systems; micro- and nanoscale systems devices and materials; energy and environment; and data analysis modeling and simulation . Hallmarks of the undergraduate experience include one full year of cooperative education, an innovative multidisciplinary senior design program, and an impressive variety of well-supported student teams and clubs.    THE UNIVERSITY AND ROCHESTER COMMUNITY: Rochester Institute of Technology is home to leading creators, entrepreneurs, innovators, and researchers. The university enrolls 16,868 undergraduates and 2,904 graduate students in more than 200 programs, and across nine academic colleges, five international campuses, as well as other degree- granting units, placing it among some of the largest private universities in the U.S. RIT is internationally recognized and ranked for academic leadership in business, computing, engineering, imaging science, liberal arts, sustainability, and fine and applied arts. RIT is also home to the National Technical Institute for the Deaf, the world’s first and largest technological college for deaf and hard-of-hearing students. With more than 900 students from around the world, NTID offers unparalleled support services for deaf and hard-of-hearing students. RIT’s cooperative education program is one of the oldest and largest in the nation. In 2019, RIT moved into the high research activity institution or “R2” category under the updated Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Learning, ranking it among the top six percent of colleges and universities in the nation for research activity. U.S. News and World Report ( USNWR ) now ranks RIT No. 88 in its “National Universities” category, and No. 5 7 and No. 6 9 for Best Undergraduate and Graduate Engineering Programs, respectively. The publication also ranks RIT No. 11 in the U.S. for co-op or internship programs, No. 48 among best-value schools, and No. 41 among most innovative. Sponsored research awards totaled $ 105 million in the fiscal year 202 5 , up from $78 million in 2018. Today, RIT counts nearly 140,000 alumni around the world. Its endowment is currently valued at $1.257 billion, and the university benefits from sound financial management. Always on the cutting-edge, RIT’s educational programs continue to evolve to meet the needs of today’s students. Building on its legacy of excellence across STEM and the arts and its commitment to developing creative thinkers, RIT launched the Performing Arts Scholars program in 2019. In fall of 2022, 482 first- year students accepted scholarships to join this program, regardless of major, bringing the total number of PA Scholars to 1,400. In support of this programming, RIT is unveiling the Student Hall for Exploration and Development (SHED) in the fall of 2023, with major facilities for the performing arts, and new classrooms, surrounding an enormous multi-story core of makerspaces. RIT has also launched a series of very successful Combined Accelerated Bachelor’s/Master’s Degree (CAB-M) programs, which attracted about 750 of the students in the fall of 2022. In addition, RIT is developing a large suite of online programs with an emphasis on upskilling for adult learners through its offerings at RIT Certified. QUALIFICATIONS:   REQUIRED: ●       Doctorate in Mechanical Engineering or closely related field ●       Ability and commitment to effectively teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students  ●       Record of disseminating scholarly research in refereed (peer-reviewed) publications   ●       Demonstrated ability or potential to establish an independent externally sponsored research program ●       Excellent communication skills ●       Ability to contribute meaningfully to the university’s continuing commitment to individual differences. ●       Interest in working in a collaborative, collegial environment HOW TO APPLY:   Candidates may apply online at http://careers.rit.edu /faculty ; select Faculty Positions, then Keyword Search.  Please upload the following documents to complete the application:   ●        Cover letter ●        Curriculum Vitae ●        Research Statement (3-page limit - include a dedicated paragraph discussing how your research will build synergy with existing efforts within the mechanical engineering department, the Kate Gleason College of Engineering, and the broader RIT campus.) ●        Statement of Teaching Philosophy (2-page limit) ●        List of three references Faculty Tenure, Rank, Discipline JC_1402 - Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering Work Location On Campus Compensation $80,000-$120,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Anticipated Start Date July 01, 2027 Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Assistant-Professor--Tenure-Track---Supply-Chain--Proj---Oper-Mgt-Quant-Meth_JR103197": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track), Supply Chain, Proj & Oper Mgt/Quant Meth",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Management Department in the Saunders College of Business at Rochester Institute of Technology invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track assistant professor of supply chain management starting August 11, 2027. Candidates who are close to completing their doctoral degree in supply chain management, operations management, logistics, sourcing, purchasing and supply management, or related areas are encouraged to apply. Assistant professors with prior experience are also encouraged to apply. Teaching load is 2/2 for pre-tenure faculty and includes teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in supply chain analytics, sourcing, logistics, operations management, decision sciences, project management, and other related areas. The ideal candidate will demonstrate the potential to produce high-quality research. Evidence of teaching effectiveness at either the undergraduate or graduate level is expected.   We are seeking an individual who has the ability and interest in contributing to a community committed to student-centeredness; professional development and scholarship; integrity and ethics; innovation and flexibility; and teamwork and collaboration. Select to view links to RIT’s core values and honor code .   To attract and retain an excellent and innovative faculty, RIT offers a number of programs and professional development opportunities to help faculty succeed from our onboarding and orientation on through to the tenure and promotion process. https://www.rit.edu/aes/ofr   THE COLLEGE/ DEPARTMENT:                                     The Saunders College of Business (SCB) is accredited by AACSB International and served by more than 60 full-time faculty members. SCB faculty greatly value collegiality and teamwork, as evidenced by the high level of collaboration within and across departments. SCB offers bachelors' degrees in Business Administration with eight different majors. Graduate programs include a Ph.D., an MBA, an Executive MBA, and Masters of Science in several disciplines. Saunders is ranked 58th by US News and World Report. The Department of Management is the largest in the college with 23 faculty members; 15 of which are tenured or tenure track. The department includes multiple disciplines: organizational behavior and leadership, strategy, supply chain management, global business, entrepreneurship, and decision sciences. The Department of Management houses BS and MS programs in Global Business Management and Supply Chain Management. Additionally, the department houses the Ph.D. concentration in Strategy and Innovation.   THE UNIVERSITY: Founded in 1829, Rochester Institute of Technology has a long-standing history of innovation that blends the arts, technology, and experiential learning. In addition to its main campus in Rochester, New York, RIT maintains a strong international presence with over 100 active global partnerships and international campuses in Croatia, Dubai, and Kosovo. Nationally recognized for its co-op and internship programs, RIT is supported by more than 4,000 dedicated faculty and staff members committed to student success. Its 1,300-acre suburban campus features cutting-edge facilities that reflect RIT’s strengths in applied research, design, and workforce development. To attract and retain an excellent and innovative faculty, RIT offers a number of programs and professional development opportunities to help faculty succeed from our onboarding and orientation on through to the tenure and promotion process.   QUALIFICATIONS:   REQUIRED: Ph.D. or ABD in supply chain management, operations management, logistics, sourcing, purchasing and supply management, decision sciences or related areas from an AACSB accredited or equivalent institution. Potential for high-impact research publications relevant to the area of specialty. Evidence of teaching effectiveness in supply chain management related areas, including supply chain analytics, operations management, purchasing, international logistics, or other related courses. Potential to collaborate within and beyond the Department of Management HOW TO APPLY: Apply online at RIT Careers ; go to Job Category, and select Faculty (Regular) to view current openings. Please submit your application, curriculum vitae, cover letter addressing the listed qualifications and upload the following attachments: A brief teaching philosophy The names, addresses and phone numbers for three references A research statement   You can contact the search committee with questions on the position at: Prof. Kevin Sweeney, ksweeney@saunders.rit.edu (Search Committee Chair) Prof. Richard DeMartino, rdemartino@saunders.rit.edu Prof. Jieun Lee, jlee@saunders.rit.edu Prof. Kalan Horton, khorton@saunders.rit.edu   A review of applications will begin immediately. For best consideration, completed applications should be received by October 30th. SALARY RANGE: $140,000 - $155,000 Faculty Tenure, Rank, Discipline JC_1413 - Assistant Professor, Prod & Op Mgt/Quant Meth /Oper Res /SCM Work Location On Campus Compensation $140,000-$155,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume, Research Statement Anticipated Start Date September 24, 2026 Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/NTID-Academic-Administrative-Support-Coordinator_JR103368": {
      "title": "NTID Academic Administrative Support Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights This position provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to both the NTID Business Studies and NTID Engineering Studies departments, including event coordination, budget and purchasing processes, student employee supervision, faculty and department chair support, technology and lab oversight, hiring and onboarding coordination, and student success initiatives. The role contributes to the effective daily operation of the department while supporting faculty, students, and institutional priorities. Sign language proficiency is highly preferred. Business Studies – Additional Responsibilities Ability to handle logistics for departmental events, o Hire, train and supervise student workers with assigned tasks for office and computer labs. o Handle the employment process for student workers with Student Employment Office (SEO). o Manage and support department chairs’ schedules and tasks o Oversee the department’s labs and office computers, monitors, printers and servers. Maintain and track inventory and equipment. o Participate in committees that are aligned to departmental and institutional needs. Engineering Studies – Additional Responsibilities o Ability to handle department budget using platforms utilized by the university. o Ability to handle logistics for departmental events o Hire, train and supervise student workers with assigned tasks for machine shop and computer labs. o Handle the employment process for student workers with Student Employment Office (SEO). o Manage and support department chairs’ schedules and tasks o Oversee the department’s labs and office computers, monitors, printers and servers. Maintain and track inventory and equipment. o Participate in committees that are aligned to departmental and institutional needs. o Coordinate all instructional material/supply purchases with Lab Technician for approval from department chair. o Maintain a Starfish Alert spreadsheet and advise the department chair if a team meeting is needed. o Update and maintain office area appearance/aesthetics for office morale and public information o Manage academic forms for registrar’s office o Prepare any summer or overload contracts for faculty as needed o Prepare and track all requisitions when new postings are to be posted, assist in setting up interviews, travel arrangements, etc. o Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education & Experience o Minimum sign language proficiency is highly preferred   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Addresses both routine and complex, unanticipated issues and inquiries, ensuring timely resolution while maintaining compliance with department and university policies and procedures. Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders on confidential matters Acts as a resource for interpreting practices, processes, and policies, providing clear guidance to others. Represents the department and program in communications with personnel at various levels, managing and safeguarding sensitive and critical information. Advises stakeholders on departmental policies and procedures Assists in the preparation and dissemination of information regarding degree programs, course requirements, curriculum updates, and marketing collateral Manages instructional support tasks such as coordinating course syllabi, administering course evaluations and exams, and responding to student inquiries Provides student services support, including processing tuition waivers, course permits, graduation checks, and tracking student progress Supports the scheduling of courses and assists with academic coordination, ensuring smooth course offerings and scheduling logistics Contributes to student recruitment efforts and accreditation activities such as data analysis, teaching assistant coordination, exam management, and helps coordinate any associated outreach events Assists faculty with grant proposal preparation, tracks grant budgets, and provides guidance on financial processes while responding to inquiries and ensuring policy compliance Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of office management, administrative procedures, and university operations to ensure effective workflow and coordination Knowledge of office software and databases, including tools for scheduling, data analysis, and managing academic records Knowledge of academic program structures, degree requirements, and course curricula to provide accurate information and support to students and faculty Skill in managing and coordinating course schedules, ensuring smooth logistics and alignment with academic calendars Skill in communication and customer service, providing clear and responsive support to students, faculty, and external partners Skill in problem-solving, addressing inquiries, and resolving issues efficiently while maintaining a high level of customer service Ability to coordinate multiple tasks and responsibilities simultaneously, ensuring deadlines are met and operations run smoothly Ability to build positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and external partners, enhancing communication and collaboration Ability to maintain accurate and organized records, ensuring that academic and financial documentation is up-to-date and compliant with university standards Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 3 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $17.90 - $28.60 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
