    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Post-doctoral-Research-in-Biology-Education-Research_JR103312": {
      "title": "Post doctoral Research in Biology Education Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights We are looking to hire a postdoctoral researcher for our NSF-funded project Tools for Teaching and Assessing Visual Literacy in Molecular Biology.  This project aims to strengthen undergraduate biotechnology education through the development of students’ visual literacy skills, a critical competency for interpreting and communicating scientific information. The postdoctoral researcher on this project will be working with research team to develop, validate, and disseminate an open-access Visual Literacy Toolkit consisting of two integrated components: the Visual Literacy Assessment for Biotechnology and a suite of Visual Literacy Instructional Materials . Project goals include identifying common visual literacy challenges, developing a reliable and valid assessment of biotechnology visual literacy, and creating instructional materials that address documented learning needs. Assessment development will include textbook analyses, expert review, student think-aloud interviews, pilot testing, psychometric analyses, and validation studies. The instructional materials will be piloted and refined through classroom implementation and instructor feedback. The project will generate new knowledge about the visual representations that are most challenging for students, the misconceptions that persist across instructional contexts, and effective strategies for teaching visual literacy as a core scientific practice. Job Summary :  The postdoctoral researcher will be involved in all aspects of the project but will primarily be working on the development, validation and testing of the Visual Literacy Assessment for Biotechnology (VLAB).   The postdoctoral researcher will engage with a vibrant community of STEM education researchers, including faculty, post-doctoral researchers, graduate and undergraduate students, who make up the Center for Advancing Scholarship to Transform Learning (CASTLE) at RIT.   The postdoctoral researcher will have the benefit of frequent interactions with all members of the RIT’s CASTLE, including weekly journal club and weekly work-in-progress meetings, both of which focus on STEM Education Research. Presently the CASTLE group is composed of faculty, postdoctoral researchers, and graduate students from biology, chemistry, physics, math and engineering education research, plus Education Research-adjacent faculty who attend periodically. Postdocs will receive guidance and training in writing from their mentors as well as getting feedback on presenting from the entire CASTLE group. The postdoctoral researcher will engage in weekly research meetings and will complete annual reviews with their mentor(s). Mentors will oversee preparation of publications and presentations that result from the work supported by the grant. Funds are available for the postdoctoral researcher to travel to conferences to present their research and network with other professionals in STEM Education. They will be encouraged to join one or more professional societies in their field of research. We will provide experience with grant writing by directly involving the postdoctoral research in proposals prepared by the mentors. Key aspects they will learn include identifying key research questions, defining objectives, describing approach and rationale, and constructing timelines and budgets. The postdoctoral researcher will have the opportunity to teach or co-teach a course or a section of a course in their discipline if it aligns with their career interests and timing. They will have the opportunity to mentor undergraduate research students who may assist, part-time with their research during the academic year. Our postdoctoral researcher will have the opportunity to take part in various professional development activities on the RIT campus. Our post-doctoral researcher will join our Access and Belonging series at RIT, to learn and practice research-based mentoring and teaching strategies. The researcher may also choose to attend workshops hosted by RIT’s Center for Teaching and Learning.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Independently conducts research including, but not limited to, constructing hypotheses, design and planning of research studies, data management, model development, conducting experiments or assessments, analysis and interpretation of results, and evaluation of research techniques Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders Ensure compliance with institutional, sponsor, and regulatory requirements Disseminates and publishes research results in peer-reviewed journals, reports, meetings, workshops, and conferences Assists in the writing of grant proposals May assist in teaching classes May mentor and assist undergraduate and/or graduate students May assist in managing research laboratories Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Demonstrated ability to plan and execute research Knowledge of applicable research methods and analytical procedures Knowledge of research compliance and ethics Knowledge of publishing/reporting requirements Excellent teamwork and communication skills Demonstrated potential for original or collaborative scholarship Scientific writing skills demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications Ability to acquire accurate, reproducible data Critical eye towards consistency, reproducibility, and the scientific method in general Excellent project and time management skills Strong interpersonal and mentoring skills Advocate for safety and ethics in the workplace Ability to communicate findings and effectively work with sponsors and stakeholders Minimum Education & Experience Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a related field Job Level Overview N/A FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $35,000.00 - $90,000.00 Annual Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/Postdoctoral-Associate_JR103301": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Hightlights The Physics Education Research group at RIT is seeking candidates for a postdoctoral researcher in quantum education who can support the goals of an NSF funded Quantum Leap Challenge Institute (QLCI): The Physics and Engineering of Practical Quantum Error Correction (PRACTIQAL). The postdoctoral associate with assist Prof. Ben Zwickl with coordinating  programmatic activities, developing curricula, and conducting education research related to quantum information science and engineering (QISE).  Primary goals of the project include increasing the accessibility of educational resources related to quantum error correction, emphasizing positive societal impacts of quantum technology within QISE education, and supporting education and training goals of the QLCI center.  A strong background in quantum mechanics and/or quantum information science and technology is required. The position will require coordinating with members across the center so strong  communication and organization skills are required. Prior experience in education research is strongly preferred. Experience with curriculum development is also preferred.       Essential Duties & Responsibilities Independently conducts research including, but not limited to, constructing hypotheses, design and planning of research studies, data management, model development, conducting experiments or assessments, analysis and interpretation of results, and evaluation of research techniques Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders Ensure compliance with institutional, sponsor, and regulatory requirements Disseminates and publishes research results in peer-reviewed journals, reports, meetings, workshops, and conferences Assists in the writing of grant proposals May assist in teaching classes May mentor and assist undergraduate and/or graduate students May assist in managing research laboratories Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Demonstrated ability to plan and execute research Knowledge of applicable research methods and analytical procedures Knowledge of research compliance and ethics Knowledge of publishing/reporting requirements Excellent teamwork and communication skills Demonstrated potential for original or collaborative scholarship Scientific writing skills demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications Ability to acquire accurate, reproducible data Critical eye towards consistency, reproducibility, and the scientific method in general Excellent project and time management skills Strong interpersonal and mentoring skills Advocate for safety and ethics in the workplace Ability to communicate findings and effectively work with sponsors and stakeholders Minimum Education & Experience Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a related field Job Level Overview N/A FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $35,000-$70,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/RIT-Academic-Advisor----Part-Time_JR102930-1": {
      "title": "RIT Academic Advisor -- Part Time",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Highlights Academic advisors function in order to support student success.  Advising is a collaborative relationship between a student and advisor.  Advisors take a student-centered approach that enriches student learning and development in preparation for success with a diverse global society.  This part time (20 hours per week) position will be assigned to the College of Science, reports directly to the Senior Assistant Dean, and works with the chair and department coordinators as appropriate. This position will develop, implement, and manage academic advisement for RIT students. The position will participate in developing strategies that will enhance retention and promote students’ connection to their academic program as well as the university.  Responsibilities: Maintain systematic and frequent contact with advisees in order to provide them with accurate information about academic progression and degree requirements, assess students’ academic progress towards degree completion, and advise students to identify barriers to success and offer appropriate referrals for academic and personal concerns. Outreach to students whenever necessary in order to assist with planning and support. Direct students towards campus resources that will enhance their ability to be academically successful, including: ASC, CRP, HEOP, Counseling Center, Disability Services, Financial Aid, and other offices. Advise students to develop their long range goals and plans of academic study, include as applicable: co-op or internship work schedules and/or study abroad opportunities. Assist students to evaluate progress towards established goals. Review and update degree audits in a timely manner, including evaluate and determine the transfer of credits; research course descriptions to determine transferability as assigned. Participate in degree certification process as assigned. Maintain awareness of institutional information including admissions requirements, new programs, course changes, deadlines, costs, expanding facilities, college-wide initiatives, transfer requirements, and relevant state and federal mandates. Keep accurate records of all interactions. Participate in university student success and retention initiatives related to advising. Collaborate with department chairs, deans’ delegates for advising, faculty advisors and university partners to ensure seamless support for students, and serve as an advising resource for faculty and staff within the college Participate in admissions and recruitment programs as assigned. Participate in orientation programs as required. Stay current with processes, technology, and computer skills relevant to advising at RIT Participate in college planning, implementation, and evaluation of the academic advisement program’s goals and objectives. Participate on departmental, college, and university committees as assigned, Participate in Advisors Council and engage in relevant professional development activities, which may include: CPD sessions, workshops, RIT courses, attendance at conferences, membership in professional organizations, etc. OTHER DUTIES AS ASSIGNED Educational Requirements: MS, MA or M.Ed in Higher Education, Counselor Education, Career Counseling, Social Work, or related field. Required Skills: Excellent listening and interpersonal skills that exhibit positive regard, care, concern, and respect for students, families, and colleagues. Strong commitment towards supporting all levels and backgrounds of students through a variety of approaches and processes to achieve their educational and personal goals. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively (written and in-person) to a broad constituency, including administrators, faculty, staff, students, and parents. Knowledge of research and theory related to college student development, including: cognitive /learning development, student persistence, student engagement, diversity and student identity, and experience applying the knowledge to support student development and success. Thorough understanding and working knowledge of FERPA regulations within a higher education setting. Working knowledge of effective decision-making and conflict resolution techniques. Nights/weekends may be required. Ability to coordinate and manage assignments in order to sustain an extensive workload within a fast-paced environment. Excellent computer skills including: SIS, Degree Audit, & related systems. Strong organizational skills. Excellent attention to details. Demonstrated ability to multi-task. Preferred Experience/Skills: Working knowledge of RIT processes, programs, and resources preferred. 2-4 years related experience in advising or a related field in higher education environment strongly preferred. Demonstrated leadership skills and experiences desired. Knowledge of deaf culture and ASL strongly preferred.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Meets with students to review degree progress and assesses progress against graduation requirements. Ensures student understand how to navigate course registration and degree requirements Monitor students’ progress. Helps students resolve requirement concerns. Identifies alternative courses and solutions to meet degree requirements. Assists students with changing course registration Reviews career goals with students and assists students with post-college planning, including reviewing and revising resumes, identifying valuable internships and fellowships, and coaching with interviews Maintains knowledge of key registration and enrollment dates. Stays current in best practices related to academic advising, student success, and higher education Makes referrals to other points of service such as counseling, financial aid, career services, student life, and disability services Conducts outreach to students to build and foster relations, provide helpful information, and ensure students are aware of available services Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of academic advising principles and practices Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication to influence and articulate a variety of topics to different and diverse audiences Skill in multi-tasking, project management, prioritization, and organization Ability to handle sensitive situations with empathy, cultural awareness, and confidentiality Ability to work independently and with a team in a fast-paced environment Minimum Education & Experience Master's degree in related field 2 years of related experience Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 2 - A fully functional role requiring established knowledge of the profession or field of work. Responsible for completing substantive assignments and projects. Problems are varied and non-routine, and resolution requires exercising judgment, analysis, advisement, creativity, and understanding broader sets of issues. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $23.80-$33 per hr. Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/RIT-College-of-Art---Design--User---Platform-Support-Technician-III_JR103220": {
      "title": "RIT College of Art & Design, User & Platform Support Technician III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The User & Platform Support Technician III is a key member of the College of Art and Design’s CADTech and Operations team, providing front-line technical, operational, and platform support for the college’s faculty, staff, students, researchers, labs, studios, and administrative areas. The position supports a diverse and specialized technology environment that includes faculty and staff computing, cross-platform (Mac/Windows) computer labs, AV systems, managed print services, tablet checkout resources, peripherals, and specialized hardware and software used in academic and research settings. Key responsibilities include: Lead, train, mentor, and supervise a high-performing team of student employees providing Tier 0 and Tier 1 front-end technology support. Coordinate daily support operations, monitor service queues and workflows, and ensure timely resolution of technical issues. Oversee the readiness and functionality of instructional labs, classrooms, and specialized technology facilities. Provide technical assistance and exceptional customer service to faculty, staff, and students in a fast-paced, service-oriented environment. Support systems administration activities, application support, user account management, and technology operations. Perform hardware maintenance, equipment troubleshooting, repair, and replacement to ensure reliable technology services. Assist with access-control systems and technology-related security processes. Develop, document, and implement procedures that support efficient and dependable technology operations across the college. Collaborate with campus partners and stakeholders to address technology needs and support changing operational priorities. Coordinate support for facilities and services that may operate beyond standard business hours. Recruit, train, develop, and retain student employees while fostering professional growth and skill development. Build positive, lasting relationships and cultivate a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive team culture. Demonstrate sound judgment, objectivity, and problem-solving skills when evaluating information and making decisions. Utilize strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills to effectively manage multiple priorities and competing demands. Promote continuous improvement through process enhancements, team development, and customer-focused service delivery. Serve as a positive role model by demonstrating professionalism, accountability, adaptability, and a commitment to excellence.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Configures, tests, deploys, and maintains Windows and Linux computer systems Manage users, computers, and security group polices in Active Directory Troubleshoots and resolves issues with hardware, software, printers, and other equipment Assists in developing, writing, and editing established technical, process, and administrative documentation Logs, documents, maintains, and coordinates the organization of a variety of data and information Maintains and tracks inventory and equipment. Ensures that assigned areas are properly stocked with supplies Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of principles and practices of computer science Knowledge of Windows Operating System Skill in a variety of programming languages, software, and systems Skill in customer service Ability to troubleshoot and problem-solve technical issues Ability to learn new technical, functional, and business concepts implemented at RIT Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 3 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 3 - Senior level role with considerable knowledge and skills. Performs complex tasks and project work. Work is typically not routine and requires troubleshooting and analysis. Mentors or guides less experienced staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $23.80-$27.50 per hour Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
