    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/RIT-Main-Location/KGCOE-Research-Program-Administration-Specialist_JR103205": {
      "title": "KGCOE Research Program Administration Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights     RIT is seeking a Research Program Administration Specialist (RPAS) to coordinate and manage a new effort at RIT to design, create, and test long and wide sheets of two-dimensional polymer (2DP) films.  Through a multi-million-dollar investment in government funding, RIT is now constructing a dedicated 2DP facility that will house a new roll-to-roll coating machine and an expanded lab to design, develop, and improve formulations to create 2DP prototypes that demonstrate feasibility for scale up to manufacturing. Although initially funded from government sponsors, we expect that the 2DP facility will grow to be a national center where 2DP materials may be developed and prototyped for commercialization to follow.  The new facility will come online in early May of 2027, but there is an immediate need now for support.  In the short term, the facility is being built, and technical staff is being hired.  Additionally, clientele for the new facility is being established now via external interactions with industry, sponsors, and academics—with a workshop being delivered in late October 2026 to create clientele for the new facility.  As such, significant administrative and logistical help is needed now as the new center is developed—to both build the effort and its administrative infrastructure, while at the same time managing a burgeoning list of clients.  Note that there is an existing effort in place now in which 2DP films are made for sponsors and industry partners with existing equipment and labs at RIT, so that effort needs to be managed while growing the new facility. In addition to these growth activities, the RPAS will be expected to coordinate the development of research proposals associated with the center in compliance with funding agency requirements, conduct financial analysis and budget management in real time, make projections that enable strategic decisions to be made regarding budgeting and projects to be undertaken, review and ensure compliance of research operations with those of various grants and external industrial partners, maintain effective collaborations with external partners and sponsors, and help the center director to manage the portfolio of research projects by providing financial, compliance, and strategic perspectives.  As the new center evolves, opportunities to advance and specialize in various other elements of the facility operation and management will become available.  As such, the successful candidate must have entrepreneurial spirit as the research effort and new facility are growing, and the candidate must be flexible to take on new challenges and responsibilities that accompany this growth.  Finally, as part of our effort, we do employ chemical engineering co-op students for three-to-six-month stints and have independent study students working with us in our lab during the school year.  We are thus seeking an individual who has the ability to work with students.  All faculty and staff in the chemical engineering program at RIT are expected to contribute to our culture of student-centeredness, professional development and scholarship, integrity and ethics; respect, diversity and pluralism; innovation and flexibility; and teamwork and collaboration. Select to view links to RIT’s core values , honor code , and diversity commitment .   REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree in related ﬁeld 8 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Commitment to student-centeredness—Candidate must support the importance of students as the primary constituency of the university. PREFERED QUALIFICATIONS: Knowledge of grant writing and proposal development that aligns with state and federal grant/sponsorship laws and regulations and RIT policies and procedures Knowledge of regulatory and compliance standards regulations Knowledge of ﬁnancial, procurement, HR, and compliance policies and procedures related to research administration Skill in project management and organization to manage schedules, resources, and project timelines efﬁciently in a dynamic environment Skill in effective communication and collaborating with internal and external stakeholders regarding complex or technical topics Ability to maintain sensitive and conﬁdential information with discretion and uphold ethical standards of grant funds Ability to manage and coordinate activities needed for the center with a wide variety of constituencies including academic, industrial and government partners THE COLLEGE/ DEPARTMENT:    The Kate Gleason College of Engineering at RIT has established its reputation as preeminent in career-oriented engineering education and applied research.  It offers bachelor’s degree programs in biomedical, chemical, computer, electrical, industrial, mechanical and microelectronic engineering, and comprehensive, innovative graduate programs in a range of engineering disciplines, with two broad-based, cross-disciplinary Ph.D. programs in Engineering and Microsystems Engineering.  Combined, discipline-specific graduate programs are in development to be launched in the near future. The Chemical Engineering Department is housed in Institute Hall, an 86,000 square foot facility with state-of-the-art labs for both faculty research and teaching.  For more information visit:   http://www.rit.edu/kgcoe/program/chemical-engineering .   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Coordinates the development of research proposals, integrating strategic financial planning and compliance with funding agency requirements Conducts financial analysis and budget management for research projects, ensuring optimal allocation and utilization of resources Reviews compliance of research operations with grant conditions, implementing changes where necessary to meet regulatory standards Establishes and maintains effective collaborations with faculty, researchers, and external partners to enhance research opportunities Manages a portfolio of research projects, providing oversight and support to ensure successful project execution Advocates for and supports the integration of new research technologies and methodologies to advance project goals Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of grant writing and proposal development that aligns with state and federal grant/sponsorship laws and regulations and RIT policies and procedures Knowledge of regulatory and compliance standards regulations Knowledge of financial, procurement, HR, and compliance policies and procedures related to research administration Skill in project management and organization to manage schedules, resources, and project timelines efficiently in a dynamic environment Skill in effective communication and collaborating with internal and external stakeholders regarding complex or technical topics Ability to maintain sensitive and confidential information with discretion and uphold ethical standards of grant funds Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 8 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 3 - A senior-level role requiring broad understanding of the profession or field of work. Independently leads diverse and often complex assignments, projects, or programs. May act as a mentor and guide less experienced staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $65,000-$90,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Evidence-Synthesis-and-Global-Education-Liaison-Librarian_JR103146": {
      "title": "Evidence Synthesis and Global Education Liaison Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Application review will begin on October 12, 2026. Reporting to the Senior Manager of Research & Instruction Services, the Research & Evidence Synthesis Liaison Librarian will establish, coordinate and anchor RIT Libraries’ new evidence synthesis service by providing expert methodological guidance, protocol development and reproducible search strategies for large-scale literature reviews. This position will support the academic and grant-writing needs of faculty, graduate students, and staff through expert consultations, advanced instruction, comprehensive literature searches and end-to-end project workflow support across multiple disciplines and colleges. This position will collaborate with colleagues across RIT Libraries and campus to design and deliver instruction, workshops, and consultations related to data literacy and responsible uses of AI in research and scholarship with an emphasis on conceptual understanding, appropriate tool selection, and responsible practice. The position will maintain awareness of evolving research, teaching, and publishing trends across disciplines and translate that awareness into responsive library services, instructional offerings and resource development.  This position also provides reference, research services, outreach and instruction to students, staff and faculty at RIT’s global campuses including RIT Dubai, RIT Croatia and RIT Kosovo by building collaborative partnerships across global campuses to ensure equitable access to research tools and instruction.  The position will develop topical and subject specific guides and incorporate innovative technologies and instructional technologies to enhance student learning and student success.   Additional responsibilities include: Provide end-to-end project management and methodological guidance for systematic reviews, scoping reviews, protocols, grant proposals and evidence-based guidelines. Design, execute, and promote high-quality comprehensive, reproducible, database-specific search strategies, including gray literature sources. Co-author, collaborate, or serve as a consultant on interdisciplinary research projects and grant proposals. Guide researchers on the ethical use of AI tools and LLMs in literature reviews, research, and scholarly publishing. Ensure best practices for the documentation, reporting, and transparency. Mentor and train library colleagues in evidence synthesis methods, search standards and best practices. Stay current with emerging developments in evidence synthesis, open scholarship, research data management, AI applications and dissemination strategies. International travel to the global campuses (approximately one trip per year on a rotating basis) may be required. Occasional weekend and non-traditional shifts will be required to accommodate time zone differences.   Additional Skills needed for this position Expertise in research methodology. Demonstrated experience with conducting primary research. Expertise in evidence synthesis search methodologies, guidelines, and standards (ex., those recommended by Cochrane, Campbell, the Collaboration for Environmental Evidence, PRISMA, ROSES). Familiarity with evidence synthesis project management tools such as: Covidence, DistillerSR, Rayyan, or others.  Demonstrated experience designing and executing complex, multi-database search strategies. Familiarity with citation management tools (e.g., Zotero, EndNote). Knowledge of ethical AI use and reproducible research practices. Experienced with the application of AI/LLMs in research workflows. Strong pedagogical and cross-cultural communication skills to deliver engaging training and outreach across multi-campus, diverse populations.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Assists students and university community members fulfill their research needs at service points Serves as a liaison for programs to promote two-way communications regarding library services, policies, and user concerns Provides informed selection, maintenance, and weeding of books, serials, databases, and other appropriate materials based on the curricular and research needs of the colleges of the programs listed Collaborates with faculty to provide curricular support and instructional sessions that support pedagogy and learning outcomes Develops relevant subjection and course-specific guidance and tutorials to assist students Stays current of new and emerging tools and technologies Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of major online information services Knowledge of data administration principles and practices Skill in assessing and integrating appropriate complex technologies into the collection and instruction programs Skill in organizational and time management Ability to explain technical concepts to audiences with a wide range of technical skills Demonstrated initiative, creativity, and a strong commitment to teaching, learning, collaboration, and public service Ability to work independently or to collaborate productively across multidisciplinary teams, colleges, and academic programs Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Minimum Education & Experience MS/MLS from ALA-Accredited Institution or Master's degree in related field 2 years of relevant experience An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 2 - A fully functional role requiring established knowledge of the profession or field of work. Responsible for completing substantive assignments and projects. Problems are varied and non-routine, and resolution requires exercising judgment, analysis, advisement, creativity, and understanding broader sets of issues. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $59,900-$70,000 annually Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Saunder-s-College-of-Business--Academic-Admin-Program-Support-Coord-IV_JR103117": {
      "title": "Saunder's College of Business, Academic Admin/Program Support Coord IV",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights This position provides support for a variety of administrative processes and projects for the Senior Associate Dean in the dean’s office. Primary responsibilities include: support of academic services and operations in the dean’s office, e.g., promotion & tenure, mid-tenure, faculty affairs, conflict of interest/training processes, accreditation, and college committee support.   Serves as primary liaison for all academic operations/services with the provost's office.   In addition, provides assessment management and administrative support for accreditation and curriculum management processes. Demonstrates initiative and leadership in facilitating communication with different stakeholders, coordinating tasks, and operating within a team-based environment by willingly providing backup for other staff in the dean’s office, as needed. Must have proven strong data management skills including proficiency with Excel, and familiarity with data analytics platforms. Hybrid Remote Work: in office 4 days per week; remote 1 day per week.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Addresses both routine and complex, unanticipated issues and inquiries, ensuring timely resolution while maintaining compliance with department and university policies and procedures. Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders on confidential matters Acts as a resource for interpreting practices, processes, and policies, providing clear guidance to others. Represents the department and program in communications with personnel at various levels, managing and safeguarding sensitive and critical information. Advises stakeholders on departmental policies and procedures Assists in the preparation and dissemination of information regarding degree programs, course requirements, curriculum updates, and marketing collateral Manages instructional support tasks such as coordinating course syllabi, administering course evaluations and exams, and responding to student inquiries Provides student services support, including processing tuition waivers, course permits, graduation checks, and tracking student progress Supports the scheduling of courses and assists with academic coordination, ensuring smooth course offerings and scheduling logistics Contributes to student recruitment efforts and accreditation activities such as data analysis, teaching assistant coordination, exam management, and helps coordinate any associated outreach events Assists faculty with grant proposal preparation, tracks grant budgets, and provides guidance on financial processes while responding to inquiries and ensuring policy compliance Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of office management, administrative procedures, and university operations to ensure effective workflow and coordination Knowledge of office software and databases, including tools for scheduling, data analysis, and managing academic records Knowledge of academic program structures, degree requirements, and course curricula to provide accurate information and support to students and faculty Skill in managing and coordinating course schedules, ensuring smooth logistics and alignment with academic calendars Skill in communication and customer service, providing clear and responsive support to students, faculty, and external partners Skill in problem-solving, addressing inquiries, and resolving issues efficiently while maintaining a high level of customer service Ability to coordinate multiple tasks and responsibilities simultaneously, ensuring deadlines are met and operations run smoothly Ability to build positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and external partners, enhancing communication and collaboration Ability to maintain accurate and organized records, ensuring that academic and financial documentation is up-to-date and compliant with university standards Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 7 years of related experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 4 - Advanced or lead role with deep subject matter expertise and/or functions as a formal or informal team lead. Leads challenging and non-routine tasks, assignments, and projects, often coordinating across teams and developing new methods or techniques. Mentors less experienced staff and reviews or delegates work. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $21.65-$30 per hour Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Re