    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Proposal-and-Contracting-Specialist_JR102982": {
      "title": "Proposal and Contracting Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Partner with faculty, researchers, and external stakeholders to identify and pursue sponsored research funding opportunities that advance RIT's research mission. Support the development of strategic partnerships by identifying funding opportunities, cultivating relationships, and connecting faculty with appropriate sponsors and collaborators. Maintain and prioritize a portfolio of funding prospects, industry partners, and research opportunities to maximize engagement and research growth. Facilitate collaboration across RIT research programs, leveraging existing strengths to expand interdisciplinary partnerships and build future research capacity. Assist faculty in securing corporate and external support for research initiatives, including guidance on intellectual property considerations and partnership development. Collaborate closely with Sponsored Research Services and other campus partners to support compliant proposal development, submission, award management, subaward processing, and post-award customer satisfaction. Sponsored Research Services The Office of Sponsored Research Services supports RIT's research enterprise by fostering strategic partnerships, advancing sponsored research opportunities, and ensuring compliance throughout the research lifecycle. The department works collaboratively with faculty, researchers, industry partners, and funding agencies to cultivate new opportunities, secure external funding, and promote innovation. Through expert guidance in proposal development, award administration, subaward management, and research partnerships, the team helps expand RIT's research impact and strengthen its reputation as a leading research university.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Creates a broad range of materials for research grant proposals including budgets, budget justifications, and letters of support Assists in creating and growing partnerships with other organizations and universities to display RIT research capabilities Serves as liaison between in-country partner institutions, program administrator, and other internal stakeholders. Establishes connections with in-country partner institutions such as universities and incubators Maintains detailed records of all correspondence with in-country partner institutions. Makes recommendations to program administrator and other internal stakeholders regarding the most efficient and effective ways to promote successful creation of circular entrepreneurs Assists in planning and managing events in support of grant-funded objectives Creates and submits proposals and develops requirements document and timeline for preparation of materials. Audits materials to ensure compliance with sponsor requirements Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of state and federal grant/sponsorship laws and regulations and RIT policies and procedures Knowledge of RIT research opportunities and programs to effectively navigate and identify opportunities Knowledge of financial, procurement, HR, and compliance policies and procedures related to sponsored projects Skill in contract management and negotiation Skill in effective communication and collaborating with internal and external stakeholders regarding complex or technical topics Ability to establish and maintain strong, productive relationships with stakeholders, fostering connections that drive business development Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 2 - A fully functional role requiring established knowledge of the profession or field of work. Responsible for completing substantive assignments and projects. Problems are varied and non-routine, and resolution requires exercising judgment, analysis, advisement, creativity, and understanding broader sets of issues. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $59,900.00 - $95,800.00 Annual Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Financial-Assistant_JR102980": {
      "title": "Financial Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights This role supports the financial operations of RIT Club Sports , working closely with student-athletes, club officers, coaches, Recreation and Wellness staff, university departments, and external vendors. It offers a unique opportunity to combine financial administration with student engagement, helping ensure the success of a vibrant and active club sports program. The successful candidate will contribute directly to the student experience by overseeing purchasing, travel expenses, reimbursements, payroll-related documentation, and financial reporting for Club Sports. This position is ideal for individuals who enjoy detail-oriented financial work while building strong relationships and providing exceptional service to students, coaches, and campus partners. Key responsibilities include: Support the financial operations of RIT Club Sports by managing budgets, purchasing, travel expenditures, and financial transactions that enable student-athletes and clubs to participate and compete successfully. Partner with student leaders, coaches, and Recreation and Wellness staff to ensure compliance with university financial processes while providing outstanding customer service and guidance. Gain valuable experience in higher education finance, budgeting, procurement, and financial reporting while working with a wide range of campus stakeholders. Play a key role in enhancing the student experience by supporting one of RIT's largest student engagement programs through efficient and accurate financial administration. Recreation and Wellness Recreation and Wellness at RIT provides opportunities that foster healthy lifestyles, personal growth, leadership development, social connection, and sportsmanship through innovative programs, services, facilities, and employment opportunities. As part of Recreation and Wellness, the Club Sports program offers students opportunities to participate in competitive and recreational sports while developing leadership, teamwork, and organizational skills. The Club Sports program supports a diverse collection of student-led teams that compete locally, regionally, and nationally. Through collaboration with student leaders, coaches, and campus partners, Club Sports creates meaningful experiences that enhance student engagement, belonging, and overall well-being. Recreation and Wellness is committed to creating one of the nation's most engaged campus communities through inclusive, innovative, and high-quality recreational opportunities.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Tracks spending, ensuring all financial activities align with university priorities and guidelines Records and processes day-to-day financial transactions. Collects and maintains accurate financial records and data in compliance with RIT policies and local, state, or federal regulations Conducts financial analyses for special projects and provides detailed reporting on expenses and budget variances Coordinates procurement activities in support of the financial operations Supports human resources and financial administration by preparing and processing relevant documentation, ensuring accurate payroll and benefits records Ensures timely and accurate financial reporting and forecasting by collaborating with departmental teams, enabling effective budget management and strategic decision-making Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of accounting, finance, and budgeting practices and protocols to ensure accurate financial management and compliance Knowledge of enterprise-wide financial applications and Microsoft Office Skill in analyzing financial data and preparing detailed reports to support decision-making and budgeting activities Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication and customer service Ability to maintain organized and accurate financial records, ensuring all transactions are properly documented and tracked Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality when handling sensitive information Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 2 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 1 - An entry-level role building knowledge and skills. Performs routine, well-defined, easy-to-understand tasks that can typically be learned in a short period of time. Work is performed under close supervision using clearly prescribed methods and detailed instructions. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $17.90 - $22.85 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
