    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Rochester-NY/Director-Campus-Planning--Design---University-Architect_JR103007": {
      "title": "Director Campus Planning, Design & University Architect",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Lead a talented and engaged team in a department that values innovation, collaboration, and service excellence. As a member of the Facilities Management Services (FMS) leadership team, you will help shape the future of RIT's campus through strategic planning and design, employee development, and organizational leadership. The Director of Planning & Design leads the planning and design activities associated with university-wide space planning, renovation and capital programs, serving as the University's architectural representative by providing design leadership and oversight for more than $20 million in annual capital construction and renovation projects. In partnership with campus stakeholders, this role develops long-range programmatic and facility plans that support RIT's strategic vision. Benefits Eligible for RIT's comprehensive benefits program, including: Medical, dental, and vision coverage Sick and vacation time 12 paid holidays per year Retirement and financial planning resources Educational benefits for employees and dependents Employee wellness program Free use of on-site fitness facilities Facilities Management Services (FMS) Planning & Design Services FMS supports the RIT community by designing, constructing, operating, and maintaining a high-quality, cost-effective campus environment. The FMS Planning & Design team shapes the future of RIT's campus through the space management, planning, design, and execution of renovation, capital, and infrastructure projects that support academic, research, residential, and administrative spaces. Working collaboratively with colleges and departments across the university, the team develops innovative solutions that align with RIT's strategic priorities and enhance the campus experience for students, faculty, staff, and visitors.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Manages planning and design activities including staff supervision, customer service, quality performance Collaborates with senior leadership to evaluate campus space needs, provide expertise, and plan for new and renovated space Oversees the design and development of campus capital projects using internal resources and external consultants, including the development of programmatic needs, basic aesthetic characteristics, and establishing project budgets and schedules Coordinates with Project Managers and customer contacts to ensure programmatic needs, design criteria, and schedules and budgets are met throughout the development of design Develops and revises processes and procedures to support collaboration across the university and provide excellent customer service Contributes to departmental strategic planning and continuous improvement Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of design and construction industries Knowledge of relevant federal and state rules and regulations Skill in project management Skill in effective communication, both written and oral Ability to plan and delegate the work of others and train and/or supervise the work of others Ability to establish program goals and objectives that support the strategic plan and plan, implement, and evaluate programs Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 15 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience & education may be considered NYS Architect License Job Level Overview Management and People Leadership Level 3 - Heads a department, multiple smaller functions with a department, or a specialized function with institution-wide span. Integrates strategic thinking to drive cross functional initiatives to optimize efficiency, performance, and innovation. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $130,800-$155,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
